WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.100
Mask R-CNN.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:08.100
Take Faster R-CNN and add one small head, and boxes become pixel-accurate shapes.

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.067
Detection says a ship is somewhere in this rectangle.

4
00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:17.400
Mask R-CNN says something sharper: these exact pixels are ship number three.

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.300
That upgrade is called instance segmentation.

6
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.967
Here is the architecture.

7
00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:28.000
Start with Faster R-CNN, which proposes regions on a shared backbone.

8
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.400
Each region's features are extracted.

9
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.667
One head still classifies and refines the box.

10
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:42.933
A second, small convolutional head, in parallel, outputs a twenty eight by twenty eight mask: which pixels inside this box belong to the object.

11
00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.033
One technical fix was essential.

12
00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:49.926
RoI pooling snapped region coordinates to the feature grid.

13
00:00:49.926 --> 00:00:52.667
That rounding is harmless for classification.

14
00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:54.700
But it smears per-pixel masks.

15
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:01.867
RoIAlign samples with bilinear interpolation instead, with no rounding, so masks stay pixel accurate.

16
00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:04.300
Now in torchvision.

17
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.167
We run the pretrained model, which returns masks along with boxes and scores.

18
00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:16.300
Keep the confident detections and threshold each mask at zero point five, giving booleans at full image size.

19
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.533
Summing one mask counts the pixels in that instance.

20
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:22.219
Why bother with masks?

21
00:01:22.219 --> 00:01:23.300
Think wildfires.

22
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.033
A wildfire is flagged, and the agent pulls satellite tiles of a wind stretched burn scar.

23
00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:33.067
A bounding box around it might be sixty percent healthy forest.

24
00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:41.267
Masks trace the real boundary, so summing pixels times area per pixel gives a defensible burned area for each fire front.

25
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:43.231
To recap.

26
00:01:43.231 --> 00:01:46.967
Mask R-CNN is Faster R-CNN plus a mask head.

27
00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.500
It gives per pixel instance segmentation.

28
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.067
RoIAlign keeps those masks accurate.

29
00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:58.130
And the design lesson: a shared backbone with cheap parallel heads.

30
00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.367
Next up: IoU, NMS and mAP.
